        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.33.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.33.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 33:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.33.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.33.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " Almighty said, “In this land that is like a desert and where no people or animals live, there will once again be pastures where shepherds can take their sheep. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.33.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.33.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 33:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In the towns of the hill country, in the foothills, and in southern Judah, in the territory of Benjamin, in the villages round Jerusalem, and in the towns of Judah, shepherds will once again count their sheep. I, the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.33.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.33.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", have spoken.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.33.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.33.13"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
